  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\n\nThe sfc high ridge axis will traverse the forecast area early Friday \nmorning. While we see some clouds linger in the early morning hours, \ntemperatures cool significantly to the upper 20s for areas \nalong and northwest of a line from Alma to Kearney to Central \nCity, while temperatures hover around the freezing mark for the \nremainder of the area. Now is a good time to disconnect any \noutdoor hoses and insulate any exposed pipes/infrastructure. \nTemperatures should warm back up to the upper 40s to low 50s by \nFriday afternoon.\n\nModels suggest another shortwave trof approaching from the west late \nFriday into Saturday. However, guidance is struggling in generating \nmuch precip, likely due to some influence of a sfc high in the \nregion. Mid level ridging builds in for Sunday with dry conditions \nprevailing. Monday into Tuesday will see another shortwave eject \nfrom southwest Canada toward the Northern Plains. At this time, the \nbest synoptic scale forcing for ascent appears well north of the \narea leading to a dry forecast. Temperatures largely remain in \nthe 60s from Saturday through Tuesday.",
